  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "Flame surges, puff paths, spark spray and the scorch's texture and angle vary per cast. The 0.2 s kindle, the ignite time and the 0.11 s reach stay fixed so the hit always lands at the same moment."
  },
  "director_notes": "A flamethrower-style jet, built to sit next to Dragon Breath without repeating it: Dragon Breath is a heavy creature breath (0.5 s inhale, wide cone at spread 3.8, sweeping across an area); this is a quick hand-held attack aimed at one target. Choices: (1) a short 0.2 s kindle (a flicker of fire at the hand, a few sparks) so it feels snappy; (2) a tight fire beam (spread 2, width 18-20 px) with fast flow (8) and high churn (0.6) so surges visibly race down the column, no sweep; (3) a compact splash at the target (additive billows, ember spray at the hit point) over a burn patch that cools into a small scorch. Hero view is side because the jet reads best in profile. Sound: ignite, a slightly higher-pitched fire hiss for the stream, a quiet fire tail."
}
